WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:04.260
Changes in your diet not
only affect you physically,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.240
physiologically inside,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.000
but also mentally,
how well you think,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.520
psychologically,
how well you feel.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.580
But you’ll never know just
how good you can feel

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.500
until you put it to the test
and try eating healthy.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.780
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.420
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.530
Today we look at the relationship
between diet and inflammation.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.020
And we start with a story
about the best ways

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.910
to alleviate chronic
pain syndromes.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.660
Fibromyalgia is a common disorder

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.740
whose cardinal manifestation
is chronic, widespread pain.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.360
Well, not so common, affecting
2 to 4% of the population

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.200
though probably more like
2%, and especially women.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.000
For decades, some medical
professionals dismissed fibromyalgia

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.960
as all in people’s heads, but this
outdated view has been refuted

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.780
by more recent research
characterizing it as a disorder

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.820
of pain regulation and sensitization.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.960
Brain imaging studies have shown
several perturbations of pain

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.660
processing and regulation
that amplify pain

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.800
in people with the condition.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.240
Twin studies have shown that about
half of fibromyalgia is genetic,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.460
but the other half we
can do something about.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.340
There are lots of drugs with
lots of side effects to help

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.340
with some of the symptoms, but
what about lifestyle approaches?

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.060
Engagement in regular
physical activity is considered

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.200
imperative for effective
management of ﬁbromyalgia.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.660
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.520
of randomized clinical
trials on the

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.280
effectiveness of therapeutic
exercise in fibromyalgia

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.460
found that both aerobic
and resistance exercises

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.800
are effective ways of reducing pain

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.700
and improving global well-being
in people with fibromyalgia.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.980
Patients may worry and
perceive that exercise

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.020
will worsen their pain and fatigue,

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.960
and so you have to start slow and
work your way up as tolerated,

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.680
with the goal of eventually
achieving 30 to 60 minutes

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.880
of moderate intensity aerobic
exercise in addition to

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.620
muscle strengthening exercises
(1 to 3 sets of 8–11 exercises,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.460
8–10 repetitions with
a load of about 7 pounds

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.680
or 45% of the max you can lift.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.980
But what about dietary
interventions in terms of

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.200
dialing down the pain sensitivity?

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.120
Well, what causes it in the
first place? Inflammation.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.080
During the inﬂammatory response,
pain receptors are activated,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.620
and chronic inflammation,
can cause chronic activation,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.040
which may cause chronic
pain, due to this prolonged

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.860
hypersensitization
of pain pathways.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.880
No wonder, then, that
a pro-inﬂammatory diet

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.400
was found to be associated
with pain hypersensitivity

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.800
in patients with
fibromyalgia syndrome.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.640
Exactly which foods
are pro-inflammatory

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.980
and which foods
are anti-inflammatory?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.520
Check out those twin videos,
but broadly speaking

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.220
components of processed
foods and animal products,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.560
such as saturated fat,
trans fat, and cholesterol,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.480
were found to be
pro-inflammatory,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.300
while constituents
of whole plant foods,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.320
such as fiber and phytonutrients,
were strongly anti-inflammatory.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.860
The intake of dietary fiber,
found concentrated in

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.840
only one place—
whole plant foods—

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.500
is fundamental to reducing not
only the risk of abdominal pain

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.180
but also muscle and joint pain,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.060
we think because of these
short chain fatty acids

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.060
that our good gut bugs
produce when we eat fiber.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.360
These short chain fatty acids
are important mediators of pain,

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.540
fundamentally because
they modulate inﬂammation.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.260
So having a lot of fiber-feeding
bugs in your colon is like

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.140
carrying around your own anti-
inflammatory compound factory.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.720
But to cultivate them you actually

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.760
have to eat the
foods that feed them.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:50.400
And in terms of phytonutrients,
plant-derived polyphenols

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.460
are widely acknowledged to also
act as anti-inﬂammatory substances.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.000
Here’s some foods packed with
anti-pain pathway nutrients:

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.880
berries, greens, citrus, nuts,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.420
spices like turmeric and ginger,
edamame, and green tea.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.780
That’s why you can do randomized,
double-blind crossover trials

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.240
showing that about three cups
worth of strawberries a day

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.060
can significantly improve
pain and inflammation.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.640
If that’s what a
single plant can do,

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.820
what about a diet chock
full of plant foods?

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.180
Put people on a strictly
plant-based diet rich in

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.760
fresh fruits and vegetables, whole
grains and various legumes,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.920
which are beans, split peas,
chickpeas, and lentils,

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.500
as well as nuts and
seeds, and you can drop

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.280
C-reactive protein
levels 33% in 3 weeks,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.400
which is a leading blood marker
of systemic inflammation.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.940
But does that translate
into less pain?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.620
And the answer is yes, when it
comes to migraine headaches.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.960
Yes when it comes
to painful periods.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.800
A signiﬁcant reduction in menstrual
pain, duration of pain, intensity

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.600
in addition to
premenstrual symptoms.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.660
In fact even just a
single plant, cinnamon,

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.300
about a third of a teaspoon three
times a day during your period

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.660
can help, though it doesn’t
work as well as ibuprofen.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.700
Ginger powder,
on the other hand—

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.200
ground ginger – has been found

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.840
to be comparable to
ibuprofen in relieving pain

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.340
in women with painful cramps.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.880
You can learn more in
my video on the topic.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.100
Whole-food plant-based
diets also alleviate

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.960
the symptoms of osteoarthritis.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.200
Several studies have shown
improvements in rheumatoid arthritis

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.360
symptoms with diets
excluding animal products,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.880
though it may be just
as much a function of

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.040
increasing the quantity
of healthy plant foods.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.980
But it’s not just because plant-
based diets are so effective

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.440
in causing weight loss,
even at the same weight

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.780
there’s an improvement
in rheumatoid arthritis

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.760
from more plant-based diets.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.900
And plant-based diets can also
alleviate fibromyalgia symptoms.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.920
This is the latest study,
which enrolled anyone

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.100
with chronic musculoskeletal
pain, fibromyalgia or not.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.120
Yes, diets high in animal proteins
and fats have been linked to

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.700
chronic pain and inﬂammation,
while plant-based diets

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.500
produce anti-inﬂammatory responses.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.920
So, did it actually work when
put to the test for pain?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.000
Yes.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.700
Consumption of a
plant-based diet produced

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.860
positive improvements
in chronic pain and function.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:05.820
How much?

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.240
Well, a minimally clinically
important diﬀerence in

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:12.540
chronic musculoskeletal
pain is 1 point on the

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.600
Numeric Pain Rating Scale,
which is just a scale of 1 to 10,

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.280
on how much pain you’re feeling.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.020
And on the plant-based diet

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.300
perceived pain
decreased an average of

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.040
three points on
a 10-point scale,

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.100
from an average of 5 or
6 out of 10 down to 2.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.120
Now, unlike most of prior studies
there was no control group,

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.420
but what’s the downside of
giving healthier eating a try?

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.420
In fact, those with chronic pain
are more likely to be overweight

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:40.260
and have nutrition-related maladies
such as high blood pressure,

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.560
diabetes, and heart disease
all of which can be prevented,

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.020
arrested, and in some
cases even reversed

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.700
with a healthy-enough
plant-based diet.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.720
So, any pain benefit is just
icing on the cake of health.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.940
Uh...scratch that.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:54.660
How about...

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:59.515
the dollop of guacamole
on your bean burrito.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.620
In our next story,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.780
we look at how plant based
diets may be effective

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:05.520
in the treatment
of fibromyalgia—

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.280
a condition suffered
by millions.

00:07:09.111 --> 00:07:12.120
According to the latest review
on fibromyalgia and nutrition,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.960
a vegetarian diet could have
some beneficial effects,

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.140
but based on what kind of evidence?

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.840
Well, back in 1991,

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.420
a survey was sent
to a few hundred folks suffering

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.960
from various chronic pain conditions
including fibromyalgia,

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.680
asking if they found any success
trying different diets.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.740
Some folks tried a vegetarian diet,
some folks tried a vegan diet.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:39.420
Some reported the various diets
helped with pain, stiffness, and swelling.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.540
Vegan diets were reported
to reduce disease symptoms

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.900
more effectively than the vegetarian diet
with rheumatoid arthritis.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:51.120
But what we needed was to put these diets
to the test in formal studies.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.180
The first one was in ’93.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:58.980
Ten fibromyalgia patients were put on
a vegetarian diet for three weeks.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:03.720
The measured levels of oxidation
and inflammation and cholesterol went down

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:04.380
– no surprise.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.900
But of interest
from a clinical point of view

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:12.180
is the positive effect of the treatment
upon pain status of most of the patients.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.780
Seven out of ten felt better.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:17.820
They weren’t sure

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.340
if it was the improved condition
of the fibromyalgia patients

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.620
in this course of treatment
with a vegetarian diet –

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.980
whether it was due to the improvement
of their antioxidant status

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:30.060
or what it was about a meat-free diet
that seemed to help so much.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:35.700
A vegan diet was first put to the test
in 2000, in Helsinki.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:41.340
You can tell English is not the researchers’
first language with sentences like:

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.680
“Plants face heavy load of light.”

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.440
The point they’re making is good though.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.440
UV light generates free radicals
in their tissues.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:53.220
All this means is that, you know,
plants must be well prepared

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.980
to meet the challenges
of the oxidant radical stress

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:00.000
and contain a broad variety
of antioxidants.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.780
That’s why plants don’t get sunburned
and their DNA damaged

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:07.260
hanging out all day in the sun
without any sun block on.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:12.780
So what would happen if you had people
live exclusively on plant items?

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.740
In other words, what might be the effects
of a strict vegan diet

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.320
on the symptoms of fibromyalgia?

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:23.160
In fact the study used a raw vegan diet.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.700
The rheumatoid patients said
they felt better

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.620
when they started to eat
the living food diet,

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.080
and the symptoms got worse
when they returned back

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.880
to their previous omnivorous diet.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.880
But what about the fibromyalgia patients?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.740
Both groups reported having
quite a lot of pain at rest

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.480
in the beginning of the study.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.320
But there’s a significant decrease
in the raw vegan group,

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.700
which gradually disappeared
after shifting back to the omnivorous diet.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.580
They also found other
significant changes,

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.260
such as improvement
in the quality of sleep,

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.940
reduction of morning stiffness,

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.400
and improvement in measures
of general health.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.200
They started out about the same,
but after about a month and a half

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.960
those eating vegan felt
significantly less stiff,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.800
which continued through the end
of the three-month study.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.660
And when they went back to eating their
regular diet, the stiffness returned.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.980
What about pains at rest?
Same thing.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.020
So significant improvements
in fibromyalgia –

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.800
stiffness, pain, and general health
on a plant-based diet.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.740
The study only lasted three months,

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.800
but it can be concluded that eating vegan

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.740
has beneficial effects
on fibromyalgia symptoms,

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.013
at least in the short run.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:42.960
Finally today,

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.740
we look at a study that suggests
chocolate may improve symptoms

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.560
for those suffering from
chronic fatigue syndrome.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:54.300
Chronic fatigue syndrome is a
debilitating condition characterized by

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:58.080
a minimum of six months of crushing
mental and physical exhaustion,

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.720
and we have no idea what causes it.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.840
We don’t even have a good idea
of how many people even have it.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:07.680
The Centers for Disease Control
estimates that as many as

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.560
seven and a half million Americans
currently suffer from it.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.220
And we as physicians have
very little to offer patients

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.320
in terms of relieving those symptoms.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.280
So, this is one of the conditions that
I’m always keeping an eye out for

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.660
in terms of new treatments.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.580
And one of the latest they
just discovered?

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:24.780
Chocolate.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.520
Evidently, Montezuma the Second,
who reigned the Aztec empire

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.940
500 years ago, noted:

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:36.240
“This divine drink, which builds
up resistance, and fights fatigue.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.360
A cup of [cocoa] permits people to
walk for a whole day without food.’’

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:44.700
Not willing to take the emperor’s
word for it, it was put to the test.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:49.200
I’m always skeptical of
industry-supported research,

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.240
but it was actually a pretty good study.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.900
At first glance, it looked like
they were basically saying eat

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.420
three chocolate bars a day for eight
weeks, and call me in the morning.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:01.980
But it was actually a randomized,
double-blind, placebo-controlled

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.320
crossover trial, which is about
as good as you can get.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:11.220
The mad scientists over at Nestle took
white chocolate, dyed it brown, and then

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:15.840
added some sort of fake chocolate
flavor, such that people couldn’t tell if

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:18.360
they were eating the
real chocolate or the fake.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:23.100
Comparable amounts of sugar and fat,
but one had cocoa solids—

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.080
phytonutrients—and the
other basically didn’t.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.160
So, they were able to put people on one,
and then switch them over,

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.480
without anyone knowing,

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:34.020
to see if their chronic fatigue
symptoms got better or worse.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.320
And there was a
significant improvement

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:41.160
in the real chocolate group,
meaning it apparently wasn’t just

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:45.420
the yummy taste of chocolate, but the
action of the cacao phytonutrients.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:49.620
Of course, no one should be eating
three chocolate bars a day,

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.980
but you can get the equivalent
dose of cocoa solids,

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.620
the equivalent dose of those
wonderful cocoa phytonutrients,

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.580
by consuming two and a half
tablespoons of cocoa powder a day.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:03.420
You can put it in coffee,
you can make a chocolaty smoothie,

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.760
or, my personal favorite,
you can blend it in a high-speed blender

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.060
with frozen cherries or strawberries,
a touch of non-dairy milk,

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.940
vanilla extract, and some
erythritol or some dates,

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:19.920
and you have instant, decadent
chocolate ice cream; low-fat,

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:23.760
low-calorie, no cholesterol,
no added sugar chocolate ice cream.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.240
The more you eat,
the healthier you are—

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:32.441
whether or not you’re suffering
from chronic fatigue.

00:13:32.718 --> 00:13:35.040
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.800
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.620
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:44.160
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.920
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.680
please go to the NutritionFacts
Podcast landing page.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.930
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.740
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:02.040
My last two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.200
and the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:07.500
Get ready this year for the
launch of How Not to Age.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.960
And, of course, all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:12.240
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.020
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.760
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:21.780
on the latest in nutrition research
with bite-sized videos and articles

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.880
uploaded nearly every day.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.400
Everything on the
website is free.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.740
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorships,

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.460
no kickbacks.

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.560
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:35.400
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.680
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:42.090
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

